{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773163979,"nonce":"y7ozWNSQOQFw7z3mKm4ILNZjTJ8=","title":"RichView: replace broken subprocess prompt path with direct PTY WebSocket write","message":"Rich view prompt submission calls sendConsolePrompt which spawns a separate `claude -p --resume ...` subprocess. This is wrong in two ways: (1) --resume requires a valid session_id from prior stream events, which may not exist; (2) the subprocess races with the already-running PTY for the same conversation state.\n\nThe PTY already runs `claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format stream-json`. Writing `prompt + \"\\r\"` to the PTY WebSocket (same as terminal view input path) submits the prompt to the running Claude TUI, which produces stream-json events that flow through handleData → feedLineParser → parseStreamJsonLine → broadcast(\"console:stream_event\") → SSE → handleStreamEvent in TerminalPane → streamEvents → StreamRenderer.\n\nFix: In handlePromptSubmit (TerminalPane.tsx), when viewMode === \"rich\", write to wsRef (PTY WebSocket) instead of calling sendConsolePrompt. Keep the synthetic optimistic display event.","files":null}]}